refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.description;
boolsem_acquire SysvSemaphoresemaphore boolnon_blocking&false;
sem_acquire by default blocks (if necessary) until the semaphore can be acquired. A process attempting to acquire a semaphore which it has already acquired will block forever if acquiring the semaphore would cause its maximum number of semaphores to be exceeded. While the call is blocked, handlers installed with pcntl_signal run only after it returns.
Any semaphore acquired but not explicitly released is released automatically, without any warning, when the SysvSemaphore object is destroyed, if auto_release of sem_get is &true;. Otherwise, it is only released when the process ends.

&reftitle.returnvalues;

 &return.success;
 If non_blocking is &true; and the semaphore cannot be
 acquired immediately, &false; is returned without any diagnostic. Any other
 failure raises an E_WARNING.

&reftitle.changelog;





    &Version;
    &Description;





    5.6.1

     The optional non_blocking parameter has been
     added; it was originally named nowait.




    8.0.0

     semaphore expects a SysvSemaphore
     instance now; previously, a resource was expected.
